; ISSUE-0037 -- Execute's own temporary file, and nothing else.
;
; The payload is built once, on the card, so that the only RAM: traffic in the
; loop is the T:TmpNNNNN file Execute creates for itself, fills a character at
; a time through the DOS buffer, and deletes (Execute.c:149-170).
;
; That temporary is the one allocation in this whole sequence whose *name
; length varies between iterations* -- it is built from the task number and
; four clock fields -- which is why it deserves isolating from ram-stress-a.
;
; The payload is comment lines, so executing it does nothing but read it.

Echo "[ram-stress-b] building the payload"
List "SYS:C" NOHEAD FILES TO "S:ram-stress-payload" LFORMAT="; %N"

Echo "[ram-stress-b] start"

Lab loop

Echo "[ram-stress-b] ."

Execute "S:ram-stress-payload"

Skip loop BACK
